### Arcade Physics Collide/Overlap with Groups

Source: https://github.com/phaserjs/phaser/blob/v3.90.0/changelog/3.2/CHANGELOG-v3.2.md

The `collide` and `overlap` methods in Arcade Physics now accept normal Phaser Groups in addition to Physics Groups, simplifying collision detection setup.

```javascript
this.physics.add.collider(groupA, groupB, hitCallback, null, this);
this.physics.add.overlap(groupA, groupB, overlapCallback, null, this);
```

--------------------------------

### Fix: Arcade Physics `collide` in `update`

Source: https://github.com/phaserjs/phaser/blob/v3.90.0/changelog/3.12/CHANGELOG-v3.12.md

Ensures that calling Arcade Physics `collide` during an `update` method correctly injects results back into the Body parent, allowing bodies to move as expected. Previously, manual checks did not work correctly, although using Colliders did.

```javascript
/**
 * Calling Arcade Physics `collide` during an `update` method wouldn't inject the results back into the Body parent, causing the bodies to carry on moving. Using Colliders worked, but manually checking did not. Now, both methods work. Fix #3777 (thanks @samme)
 */
```
